#passage(("It's not a sign. It's, with all due respect, misunderstanding. It's not about perspective. It's about objective facts. With all due respect, you're not an Arabic speaker, and the Arabic language is an objective language. There are rules. There're grammatical rulings. So when I tell you wrong based on the Arabic language, that's not a subjective opinion. You cannot come to a word, like the word كِتَاب (ketab) means Book, you cannot come and tell me the word كتاب means... my room! You cannot change language and tell me that's a subjective thing. No! There are many things which are objective, that aren't bound by interpretation, and this Verse is one of them. And therefore, it's not a perspective. It's an objective fact that the language in this case, you are misunderstanding it because you're not an Arabic speaker.", "What you just said before is essentially your Book is plagiarism, where someone has plagiarised some statements from the previous Books and came up with a Book. Now, there is two problems there. First, if it's a plagiarism of other scriptures, it's not necessary, because the information already exists in the other scriptures. I don't need to look at the plagiarism which takes information which already exists. The second problem with this plagiarism Book that you have is the fact that nobody gave that person authority, whoever collected that Book and gathered this information, to do so. Nobody has ordained him, divinely, and gave him revelation to do that thing on his own. That's why I'm telling you, it's not about perspective. It's about objective fact, that perspectives that you're bringing, it cannot work in reality.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sacred Treasurey Follower Challenges Muslim On The Final Revelation! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IwY1FORIiaU", ((604, "10:04–10:58"), (662, "11:02–11:39"),))
