#passage(("He rebuilt The Kaaba on the foundations that were there before, because The Quran3:96 says: إِنَّ أَوَّلَ بَيْتٍ وُضِعَ لِلنَّاسِ لَلَّذِي بِبَكَّةَ مُبَارَكًا (The first house to be established for the people is the one in Bakkah (ie Mecca)), which is the Kaaba. So it was established way before, and that's why The Quran2:127 says: وَإِذْ يَرْفَعُ إِبْرَاهِيمُ الْقَوَاعِدَ (When Abraham was elevating the foundations of the house). The foundations were there; he just elevated the foundations of the house. He rebuilt the house that was already there.", "It's false to say there's no historical evidence for it. The Bible mentions that Kedar, who lived in the regions where the Arabs live today, comes from Ishmael, who is the son of Abraham. So they were in that region. Ibrahim and Ismail ﷺ (peace be upon them) were in that region, and the house is built, and the Arabs trace the lineages back to Ismailﷺ. They have the whole lineages, the name of the father, the grandfather, the great great grandfather, going all the way back to Ismailﷺ. This is a pride thing within the Arabs. So there is literally traceable history, stronger than any other one, that Ismailﷺ was in that region, and his mother was in that region, and they were there and they built the house. To claim that there is no historical evidence that the Kaaba was built by Ismailﷺ is a complete rubbish, nonsense.", "You can have maybe some Roman sources and this and that; you will see them talking about that: there was a house there, there's a Kaaba, and they used to hold it to higher regard, but they used to worship idols, and The Prophet broke the idols that they used to worship, that they had around the Kaaba, over 300 Idols around the Kaaba. But they used to believe it is something that it is Holy. They used to hold it to be something holy because it was built by Abraham, according to them, and that's why, even when they wanted to rebuild it in The pre-Islamic Times, they said we don't want to use any filthy money. No money from prostitutes, no money from interest. They themselves did not want to use any money, them knowing that this money is dodgy in the sight of God. They said we want to only use good money, pure money to rebuild, because for them they knew that this was a holy site. Even the Jews would not deny this, because there was Jews that know about the Arabs.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Why Do Muslims Reject The Claim Of Paul? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HS9YyIgDMtg", ((990, "16:30–16:53"), (1045, "17:25–18:02"), (1132, "18:52–19:35"),))
