#passage(("The only history of Arabia is found with the Arabs. No one else has recorded the history of Arabia except the Arabs, and the Arabs have recorded that Abraham built the house and Ismael built the house with him, and this is what we believe. We do not need to convince anyone with anything; no one else has a historical evidence that opposes it. Because no one wrote the history of the Arabs except the Arabs, you have one of two options: either to accept the history the Arabs wrote about themselves, or to claim that we don't accept it, which then, we don't care. If someone accepts the history of the Arabs or not, it still makes it the history of the Arabs. Now, the question then should be whether the Quran is true or not, and if the Quran is true, then Abraham did build the house of God, and we are in the house of worship of God. That's it!", "But to insinuate it's Pagan, this is a different claim now than \"who built it, who didn't build it\". You insinuated things to do with Paganism, and there is no historical evidence for that. So if you talk about what the Bible says or the Bible doesn't say, where is the evidence that what the Bible says is historically reliable?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Hebrew Israelite Questions Muslim On Pagan Teachings! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wmSxtBM_0W4", ((294, "4:54–5:24"), (328, "5:28–5:38"),))
