#passage(("Now when you say these Pre-Islamic practices, you're missing one important thing there: the idea that Islam was there from the beginning, before Prophet Muhammadﷺ. So that place, the Kaaba, was there from the beginning. So it's not like this is a Pre-Islamic practice that comes from the pagan Arabs. That's what a lot of people confused! It predates the pagan Arabs, predates even Abraham ‘Alayhi salam (peace be upon him), because the House is the first House to be built for mankind. So the fact that the pagan Arabs used to hold it as a Holy place, it's not a pagan practice, because the only reason they hold it to be a Holy place was because of Abraham. And they had traces, some of the teachings of Abraham, and because Ibrahim (Abraham) ‘Alayhi salam and his son Ishmael are the ones who built the House, and the Arabs come from the lineage of Ishmael anyways, they used to hold the Kaaba to higher regard.", "So there was no polytheism in the Arabian Peninsula until one individual called عمرو بن لُحَيّ ('Amru Bin Luhayy). He traveled and he saw some of the pagan worshippers worshiping idols. So he went and he brought some of these idols, and he was respected in the Arabian peninsula, so when he brought it, he said to the people: Look! I found this very good idea: these people who were prostrating to the idols, we can do the same thing for us. We can make our own idols and prostrate to them. And this is how the religion of the Arabs was changed. The Prophetﷺ says: \"I saw 'Amru bin Luhayy in Hellfire dragging his...\" He's been punished in Hellfire. And then the Prophet said: \"أوّلُ مَن بدَّلَ دينَ العرب\" (He was the first person to change the religion of the Arabs) by bringing the Idols into the Arabian Peninsula.", "He introduced the idea of worshiping Idols, and then gradually they started making more Idols. Isaf and Naila إيساف ونائلة, for example, were 2 Idols that they used to worship, but their story is very funny. It's actually 2 people who committed fornication in the Holy place, and later on when they died, they made Idols for them and they made them righteous people and started worshiping them. So it's ridiculous how many Idols that were introduced later on. What 'Amru Bin Luhayy did is that he introduced the idea, because they did not have this idea of Idol Worship in their mind to begin with. He introduced the concept of making an Idol and worshipping it, and then all of those Idols were gradually being introduced into the Arabian peninsula.", "Arabia had practices of Abraham, but yes, they were Idol worshipers, they were still worshiping Idols. But the worship of The One God was always there, from the teachings of Abraham and from the teachings of Ishmael, because they were there in that region. So their teachings were still there until it was corrupted later.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Does Islam Contain Pagan Teachings? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0L6bTixTAd4", ((160, "2:40–3:37"), (221, "3:41–4:15"), (276, "4:36–5:10"), (329, "5:29–5:54"),))
