#passage(("You're confusing the Pagan Arabs with the teachings of Islam and what the Muslims were doing. These are separate things. Everything I told you now is what the Muslims were doing. We don't care about what the Pagan Arabs were doing. Yes, there were Idols around the Ka'ba, and they were not praying towards the Ka'ba; they were praying to the Idols. They believed that the Ka'ba was a holy site because there were remnants of the religion of Abraham still for the Pagan Arabs, but they had over 300 Idols around the Ka'ba and they used to pray to these Idols. They used to worship these Idols and they believed the Idols bring them closer to Allah (Azzumar39:3). They placed them around the Ka'ba. They were not a group of people coming together to pray to the Ka'ba, as Muslims now pray towards the Direction, not to the Ka'ba. So, the Pagan Arabs were Idol worshippers. They used to make Idols, have different gods that they make, demi-gods if you want to call them that, because they didn't believe they were the absolute gods.", "When I said \"First Direction\" and \"Second Direction\", I'm talking about the Muslims, what the Prophetﷺ told his followers, the people who accepted his Message. The Muslims that followed the Prophet Muhammadﷺ, he gave them the First Direction of Prayer towards Jerusalem. And then, that Direction of Prayer was changed later towards the Ka'ba. That's it!", "The Pagan Arabs did not pray like the Muslims, for example. The way we pray, the way you see us pray, none of them used to pray that way. This is the teachings of Islam. You don't imagine them going around the Ka'ba then prostrating. They were not doing that, because that was not a part of their teachings anyway. They used to go to these Idols, give them sacrifices, for example, like the normal teachings of the Pagans. They give them sacrifices or give them certain things, food, this and that. And then, they asked them for things. This is what I mean by prayer. They asked them, \"Give me 