#passage(("I don't agree with what you just said. What you just said is based on an assumption: what the Bible says, it's historically accurate, and you've not provided evidence that it is historically accurate. We don't think the Bible is historically accurate; we don't think that Jesus said that to begin with. Where is the evidence that he's said that? First, when we see established evidence that what the Bible says is historically accurate and reliable, then we can maybe talk about \"OK, and now how do we understand it?\" But this is not the case.", "We are saying that the Kaaba was built by Abraham, that's what we believe as Muslims, and he was commanded by Allah to build it. And it was originally built as the First House, built by Adam, as many scholars have noted, and Abraham built it on the foundations after it was destroyed. So Allah says in the Quran (Al-Baqaraa2:127) وَإِذْ يَرْفَعُ إِبْرَٰاهِيمُ ٱلْقَوَاعِدَ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ (when Abraham was lifting the foundations of the house), meaning that there was foundations already that he was lifting.", "So we believe that this is the house of Allah that Allahﷻ created for the act of Pilgrimage, and Pilgrimage is the act for the Creator alone. In fact, when Muslims do Pilgrimage, this is what they repeat. When we are in Mecca, when we do Pilgrimage, when we do Hajj or 'Umrah (the Minor Pilgrimage), we say that \"there is none worthy of worship or there is no partners with Allah\". This is literally what we repeat! We say: لَبَّيْكَ اللَّهُمَّ لَبَّيْكَ، لَبَّيْكَ لاَ شَرِيكَ لَكَ لَبَّيْكَ (You have no partner) إِنَّ الْحَمْدَ، وَالنِّعْمَةَ، لَكَ وَالْمُلْكَ (the Praise and Glory and all of that is only due to You) لاَ شَرِيكَ لَكَ (there is no partner). It has nothing to do with Paganism; it's the exact opposite of what Paganism is and Pagan teachings are.", "Now there were some statues that were put by the Arabs, when the Arabs became Pagan, and that happened when a person who's called 'Amr Ibn Luhai, specifically, he went, he travelled, and he went to other lands, and he saw Persians, and he saw other polytheists worshipping idols, and then he introduced idol worship into Arabia. But in the beginning there was no idol worship in Arabia. They always understood that this is the house of God that has been built by Abraham, whose son Ishmael is where the Arabs come from, and that house was for worshipping God alone. But later on this idol worship was introduced, and Prophet Muhammedﷺ completely destroyed all of these 300 Idols that were around the Kaaba when Muslims came back to Mecca and took back their houses. In fact, he told his companions, like Anas Ibn Malik, \"to not see any Idol and leave it. You have to break any Idol; if you see any Idol, break it.\" So this idea of idol worship, it is the biggest sin that Islam opposes! For someone to come and insinuate that Muslims have anything to do with polytheism is completely ridiculous from a historical point.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Hebrew Israelite Questions Muslim On Pagan Teachings! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wmSxtBM_0W4", ((81, "1:21–1:43"), (108, "1:48–2:16"), (136, "2:16–2:50"), (179, "2:59–4:05"),))
